@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy & Zero-Telemetry Transparency — SaveZonix";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"Privacy"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Effective Date: January 1, 2026</span>
                <span>Last Updated: September 15, 2026</span>
                <span>Zero-Telemetry Standards</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Executive Summary:</strong> SaveZonix is an independent Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) software utility operating on a strict zero-telemetry and local-execution privacy model. We do not sell or monetize personal data, employ third-party advertising tracking networks, or perform device fingerprinting. All video stream analysis and chunk remuxing occur directly on your local device.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>We collect only the minimum technical information required to maintain account credentials, daily download quotas, and personal history:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account Credentials:</strong> When you register, we store your full name, email address, password hash (salted via ASP.NET Core Identity PBKDF2), and registration timestamp. Passwords are never stored in plaintext.</li>
                <li><strong>Personal Download History:</strong> When signed in, your download history stores the video title, source media stream URL, resolution, format, and file size in your personal database record. This data is private to your account and can be deleted at any time.</li>
                <li><strong>Session &amp; Security Cookies:</strong> We utilize secure HTTP-only session cookies strictly for authentication integrity and anti-forgery (CSRF) protection.</li>
                <li><strong>Guest Daily Quota:</strong> For unregistered guest users, daily usage counts are stored locally in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> to enforce the fair daily limit of 5 downloads.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>2. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Zero Device Fingerprinting:</strong> We do not capture MAC addresses, hardware identifiers, WebGL/Canvas fingerprints, or unique device serial numbers.</li>
                <li><strong>Zero Unrelated Browsing Tracking:</strong> The SaveZonix browser extension activates network request inspection exclusively on video playback pages where stream manifests (HLS/DASH) are present. It never harvests or logs your general browsing history.</li>
                <li><strong>No Third-Party Advertising Trackers:</strong> There are no Google Analytics, Meta tracking pixels, or commercial telemetry beacons in SaveZonix.</li>
                <li><strong>No Credential Leakage to Media CDNs:</strong> Your SaveZonix credentials are never transmitted to third-party content delivery networks.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. User Data Ownership &amp; Erasure</h2>
            <p>You have full ownership of your data:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Download History Purge:</strong> You can clear individual download logs or wipe your entire download history at any time from your <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Downloads" class="auth-link">Downloads Dashboard</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> You may request full account deletion and data erasure by contacting our compliance desk at <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Security &amp; Encryption</h2>
            <p>All network communications between the browser, local application engine, and cloud authentication servers utilize TLS 1.3 encryption. Passwords and sensitive session tokens are protected against eavesdropping.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
